# Fail rubric (~9 quality bar)

Treat work as **failed** if any of these apply:

- Business logic in controllers, route handlers, or React pages (belongs in services / hooks)
  - **Exception:** trivial one-liner handlers may call a service directly; tiny single-file helpers may stay flat (no empty ceremony folders)
- Hardcoded user-facing UI copy (must use i18n keys)
- Access/refresh tokens in `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, or JS-readable cookies
- Ad-hoc API error shapes (must be `ApiError`: `status`, `errorMessage`, `errorCode`, `errorKey`)
- Non-`ApiError` HTTP failure bodies on API routes (including auth and rate limits)
- Secrets (passwords, tokens, cookies, authorization) leaked in HTTP errors or logs
- Non-atomic register (user + refresh + idempotency) or non-transactional refresh consume+reissue
- Treating an `Idempotency-Key` alone as authentication
- New auth/error paths without tests
- Coverage below **80%** on the scoped packages below
- `any` sprawl or unchecked deep imports across packages/modules
- New API errors without `errorKey` + i18n catalog entry
- HTTP routes outside `/api/v1/...`
- Cross-origin cookie auth without a documented exception
- New protected route without the role-check pattern (`RequireAuth` / `requireRole`)
- Critical POST (at least register) without Idempotency-Key support
- Production source maps enabled for the web app
- Secrets committed (only `.env.example` is allowed)
- Prior-account private React Query / client caches surviving login, logout, register, or identity-changing refresh
- Bounded list APIs without continuation (`nextCursor` / equivalent) when clients need complete datasets (export/editor/dashboard)
- Silently treating a truncated page as a complete export or full dataset
- Destructive bulk/key operations without confirmed user intent + ownership/authz checks
- Idempotency storage that mixes unrelated operations/accounts (unscoped keys) or returns 500 on stored shape mismatch
- Dual-backend drift: same contract endpoint with different auth cookie semantics or `ApiError` shape across tracks

## Coverage scope (explicit)

Floor applies to **lines, statements, functions, and branches ≥ 80%** on:

| Scope | What counts |
|-------|-------------|
| `@repo/contracts` | Package coverage thresholds |
| `@repo/auth` | Full package, including hooks, forms, providers, and guards |
| Active API track(s) | Package/service thresholds on the backend track(s) you changed |

Verify with:

```bash
pnpm --filter @repo/contracts test
pnpm --filter @repo/auth test
pnpm --filter @repo/api test
pnpm --filter @repo/api-python test
```

See `rule-to-check-mapping.mdc` for what CI actually enforces vs human review.
